      "summaryMarkdown": "Passed. `release-plz.toml` carries every REL-1 key: git-only, tag `v{{ version }}`, `git_release_enable = true`, `release_commits = \"^(feat|fix|perf)\"` and `semver_check = false`, both commented with the 1.x policy. The `rayx_reactive` package has root `changelog_path` and `doc-examples` has `release = false`, with no `version_group`/`changelog_include` and no dist references. `[changelog]` matches the CLI's apart from the header naming `rayx_reactive` and one `commit.footers` loop that renders `  *Migration:*`, which continues the list item in the same style as the hand-written notes. `release-plz.yml` matches the CLI's except for the `rayx-ui/RayX.Reactive` guard, `release-pr` `needs: release`, and an adapted header comment covering the PAT reason, release-plz creating the Release and tests living in ci.yml. `ci.yml` is unchanged from HEAD, and it and `release-plz.yml` are the only workflow files. Version is 1.0.0 in `[workspace.package]` and Cargo.lock, with doc-examples at 0.0.0. CHANGELOG.md starts byte-for-byte with the configured header, followed by `## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-19` and the reworded lead line. Everything from `### Delivery` on is identical to HEAD, including all 17 subsections and 11 *Migration:* notes. Dry-run copies confirm A: 1.0.0 with no changes; B: 1.0.1 with the root changelog prepended under a single header; C: 1.1.0 with Features, the rendered Migration line and no breaking marker; D: no release. Minor observation, not a defect: generated sections are dated from UTC commit time, so the previews show 2026-10-18 above the locally dated 2026-10-19 1.0.0 section.",
      "findingIds": [],
      "recordedAt": "2026-10-18T22:03:07Z"
    }
